Ports upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#64165 (merged 2026-11-11, after the 0.34.0 branch) to this pin, in place of
vllm-pr61612-flashinfer-async-barrier.

FlashInfer's plan() fills the wrapper's page-locked buffer and copies it to the GPU asynchronously. Under async
scheduling, and across pipeline-parallel micro-batches, the host could run the next plan() while the previous copy
was still reading that buffer, so a later attention kernel read a half-overwritten plan: the illegal memory access
of HyperQwen #328 (PP=2), vllm #63505 and #61239. The builder now records a CUDA event after each plan() and waits
on it before the next, so the host blocks only when it is more than one plan ahead of the GPU. The port it
replaces took the blocking seq_lens.cpu() again at every step under async scheduling.

Applied unchanged: the vllm/ hunks cherry-pick onto 0.34.0 without conflicts. The PR's test file
(tests/v1/attention/test_attention_backends.py) is not carried, as with the other backports.

Kind: fix
What: wait on a CUDA event before each FlashInfer plan() so the host never overwrites a plan buffer the GPU is
  still copying
Upstream: vllm #64165 (merged), for #63505; HyperQwen #328
Cut-against: 0.34.0
Retires-when: the pin that carries #64165 (0.35)

